    {
      "week": 3,
      "day": 16,
      "title": "Belorado -> Villafranca Montes de Oca",
  "distance": "11, km",
  "time": "2 h 58 min",
  "short_desc": "A Short walk and history in the walls.",
  "long_desc": "After two long days of walking, today’s plan was wisely kept short, just 12 kilometers, giving our tired bodies a much-needed break. The morning began with breakfast at Fernando’s, our kind host for the night. Before we left, he showed us a shortcut across his land that connected directly to the Camino trail, a thoughtful gesture that saved us both time and effort. After a morning coffee in the first village, we continued straight on to Villafranca Montes de Oca, a small town with a big historical presence. Here you’ll find Hotel San Antón Abad, originally built in the 14th century as a hospital for pilgrims. Since the 1970s, it has been transformed into a charming and comfortable hotel, complete with a restaurant, cafeteria, and bar. They offer pilgrim menus for both lunch and dinner, making it the perfect place to rest, refuel and feel the spirit of centuries of Camino history.",
